      "pattern": "\\belse\\s+if\\s*\\(\\s*(?!!)[^;{]*?\\.\\s*equals\\s*\\(\\s*\\\"[^\\\"]*\\\"\\s*\\)",
      "reason": "Java 7 added String support in the switch selector. Only an else-if branch comparing a String against a compile-time string constant is convertible to a case label; the previous run's broad '\\.equals\\s*\\(\\s*\"' pattern flagged 121 sites of which 117 were single, unchained ifs and had to be SKIPPED.",
