    "truncated": false
  },
  "rule_description": "A branch of an if / else-if chain tests a String-valued expression against a string literal with .equals(). Java 7 permits String in a switch selector, so a chain of such branches over one receiver collapses into a switch with case labels. The pattern deliberately matches only the 'else if' head of a branch (so a lone, unchained if is never flagged), requires a string-literal argument (so an .equals() against an arbitrary object is never flagged), and rejects a negated condition.",
  "rule_id": "STRINGS_IN_SWITCH",
  "rule_name": "Java 7 String in switch — if/else-if chain over String constants",
  "run_id": "jade-1.6-to-1.7-v2",
  "sample_size": 18,
